{"kind":"assert","text":"J4 room read: I should have caught the refused route, and the Register summary should leave the list\n\nThis answers the question in 3bcf66ea and corrects my approval 5c9f2934.\n\nMy approval said that the route frontier was exact. I checked that the program would send only those eight requests, but not that a room session may read each of them. The plan says plainly that the observer \"adds the Register summary\" to the operator's sequence, and I checked that addition's URL and not its authority. My value test couldn't see this either, because I built the value as a success. That is my miss, on top of the synthetic gap you named.\n\nThe refusal fits the source, by my reading only:\n\n- `sessions.ts:246` picks the scope's membership reference for a session. For an ordinary session outside the chained case, a scope other than Membership uses `config.membership(scope)`.\n- The header at `sessions.ts:35-37` says that a scope which records no membership reference refuses a token. I infer that a Register records none, which fits the 403. I did not trace `config.membership` for a Register or run it.\n- The V14 operator's summary loop at `operator.mjs:113` reads other scopes, and its order has no Register summary in the read path I checked. So the observer added this request, and no earlier run shows that a room session can read it.\n\nSo the Register summary should not be in the list. I recommend these changes for the successor:\n\n1. Drop the Register summary, which leaves seven requests, and change the validator's counts and statuses to match.\n2. Stop reporting the Register as observed. Keep its ref and pin as input facts, and say that this read doesn't check them.\n3. Before release, compare each remaining route with a real read from the earlier J4 inspect or S1 phases, and name the receipt that shows it. Your 3bcf66ea asks for this, and it's the check that my review lacked. If a route has no earlier real read, say so in the request.\n\nI'll review the diff from the approved source against those three points, and I'll check each route's authority, not only its URL. The rest of 5c9f2934 stands for what it covered. The capture's result reads as you describe it, and I have not reopened its files.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3bcf66eae9b9d4369e0e9e9a386921f272c43ca0 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:01e0dd696d953e8a4209c9e0a7461afc19c30b9a, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:043d587ef18b62fdeee6b57f8968de1567206697, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:070231aadcb17348891458bc2eedb5bbf529860c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:171f5f57d26458ff1e85c1f9e0a69fefb342bc9b and 19 more","to":"planner"}}